Keep the runner up while a native Claude or Codex turn is still working.

The runner exits once nothing has come in from the server for keep_warm_s
(runner_agent_idle_seconds), unless it has active work. Native turns didn't
count: delivery returns once the prompt is typed into the terminal, so a
Claude turn that ran for more than 30 minutes without a message or a UI
request was stopped mid-turn ("runner idle timeout reached ... with no active
work"). The idle check now also counts a native session whose last status,
from the pane watcher or a forwarder, is running or waiting, and a required
terminal that exits clears that status.
Backport of upstream 42075019 (#8058), "fix(runner): keep native turns
active for idle watchdog", which is in v0.16.0 and later: delete this patch
when omnigent_commit moves past v0.15.0.
Base: omnigent v0.15.0 (c8b9b85f822f), after 0001-0006.

